## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
AVGO operates as a fab-lite company, outsourcing manufacturing to TSMC and others. This reduces capital intensity but increases dependency on foundries during capacity crunches. The company is well-positioned in the data center market (Google, Meta) but faces inventory digestion risks amid macroeconomic uncertainty.  

**Severity:** **MEDIUM** — Dependency on external fabs and concentration in data center markets create moderate risk during cyclical downturns.  

